findings.suggested_fix:
Never hand the shared context to a connection that will mutate it. Minimal change in _urllib3_request_context: use the preloaded context only for the plain case and fall back to the old ca_certs path otherwise:

    elif verify is True:
        if client_cert is None:
            pool_kwargs["ssl_context"] = _preloaded_ssl_context
        else:
            pool_kwargs["ca_certs"] = extract_zipped_paths(DEFAULT_CA_BUNDLE_PATH)

(and combine with the finding above so subclass-supplied ca_certs/ca_cert_dir/ca_cert_data also take the ca_certs path). If the mTLS case must stay fast, keep a lock-protected dict of contexts keyed by (cert_file, key_file) instead of sharing one. Add a test: perform a verify=True request with cert=... against the mTLS TLSServer, then a second verify=True request with cert=None against a CERT_OPTIONAL server and assert the handler's sock.getpeercert() is None.
